  "persona": "",
  "subject": "a retired farmer in Zuojhen, Tainan, who walks the dry white riverbed of the Tsailiao Creek every winter with a small hammer looking for fossils, is called mad by the village until the young woman at the local fossil museum identifies his find as a rhinoceros tooth and writes his name under it, and now leads a line of children with toy hammers",
  "caption": "Taiwanese Hokkien cumbia in the classic Mexican-Colombian dance-hall style. A button accordion playing bright, bouncing riffs; a güiro scraper ticking on every beat; congas and timbales with fills into each chorus; a round electric bass on the two-note cumbia pattern; clean electric guitar chops on the offbeat. Bright, dry, live-band mix with the accordion up front. A warm, slightly raspy male baritone telling the story with a grin, children's voices joining on the last chorus. 98 BPM, D major. Sunny, stubborn and warm-hearted. No reggaeton dembow, no trap drums, no autotune, no EDM drop, no rap verse, no pop ballad chorus.",
  "lyrics": "[Verse]\n透早 阿土伯 戴一頂竹笠仔\n手攑一支 細支的鐵鎚仔\n菜寮溪 寒天水焦焦\n白色的溪埔 伊一步一步看\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n人講伊老矣 頭殼歹去\n伊講石頭內底 有物件咧等\n\n[Chorus]\n敲一下 叩叩叩\n土底的骨頭 咧應伊\n幾十萬年 才等著今仔日\n阿土伯 來揣你轉去\n\n[Verse]\n有一工 鐵鎚敲著 一粒硬硬的\n一支牙 比伊的拳頭閣較大\n伊用面巾 包甲密密\n騎鐵馬 載去庄內的化石館\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n館內的小姐 目鏡戴起來\n看一下講 這是犀牛的牙\n\n[Chorus]\n敲一下 叩叩叩\n犀牛 佇遮行過路\n幾十萬年 才等著今仔日\n簿仔頂 寫阿土伯的名\n\n[Verse]\n這馬伊的後壁 綴一陣囡仔\n逐个攑一支 塑膠的鐵鎚仔\n伊教 敲毋通傷大力\n看著白色的 就喝伊來看\n\n[Bridge]\n伊坐佇館內 看玻璃櫥仔\n犀牛牙下底 一張細細的紙\n寫的是 伊的名\n\n[Chorus]\n敲一下 叩叩叩\n囡仔喝甲 規溪埔攏聽著\n幾十萬年 才等著今仔日\n明年寒天 閣來揣你\n\n[Outro]\n叩 叩 叩",
